    {
      "id": "skarn_bel_tally_gave",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "It is a folded sheaf, tied. “Every day, the count and the state of it,” Bel says. “Four hands and the same two things written down over and over: nine hundred and one, and already clean.” A pause. “If you find the extra one, do not tell the hold before you tell me.”"
        }
      ],
